6RFmyk=/1920x1080/smart/2022/11/09/181945-1668017985490.jpg\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" id=\"item03\" alt=\"Illustration of a heart cut out of military camouflage \"> </td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.3\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#848484\"> <p>Illustration: Natalie Peeples/Axios</p> </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><p><strong>Tonight's dose of kindness </strong>comes from reader Billy Guice, who lives in Mississippi's Biloxi-Gulfport area, home to Keesler Air Force Base and the Naval Construction Battalion Center.</p><ul><li><strong>\"When possible at lunch,</strong> I try to pick up the tab for a table of men and women in uniform, anonymously if possible. I ask that the establishment simply say, 'Thank you.'\"</li></ul></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48296683.351325/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtZmluaXNoLWxpbmUtNzZhOWEzZWYtMTllOC00NWE1LTk1M2QtOGNkZWYxZjc1Nzk1Lmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QyJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkyJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aC8faf63b9\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48296683.351325/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_dGV4dD0lRjAlOUYlQUElOTYlMjBQaWNraW5nJTIwdXAlMjB0aGUlMjB0YWImaGFzaHRhZ